# Copy to .env and fill in whichever of these you want. .env is gitignored.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. With no .env at all, `--offline` runs the whole
# product: the real hypotheses, the real movement code, the real terrain
# arrays, the real field and the real evidence filter, executed locally against
# the committed fixtures. That is what `docker compose up` and the test suite
# both do, and it is the mode to start in.
#
# Each key below buys back one piece of the live path. They are independent:
# supplying one and not the others works, and the missing piece falls back.


# --- SEARCHLIGHT_OFFLINE ---------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Default 1 in Docker, 0 outside it. Set to 0 to use the live fleet
# and the model calls; any key that is still missing falls back on its own.
#
#   SEARCHLIGHT_OFFLINE=1


# --- DAYTONA_API_KEY -------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. https://www.daytona.io
#
# Buys: the simulations run in isolated sandboxes instead of in the
# orchestrator's own process. This is what makes it safe to execute
# model-written movement code, and it is why the offline fleet declines a
# generated script rather than running one locally.
#
# The dashboard also shows the account's concurrency ceiling. This account's
# tier caps TOTAL cpu at 10 and TOTAL memory at 10 GiB across all live
# sandboxes, so a 1 GiB worker gives a fleet of 10 and a 2 GiB worker gives 5.
# See orchestrator/settings.py.
#
DAYTONA_API_KEY=


# --- OPENAI_API_KEY --------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. https://platform.openai.com
#
# Buys three things, each of which degrades on its own:
#   1. Hypotheses specific to this terrain, rather than the five published
#      ISRID family names. The family WEIGHTS always come from
#      data/priors.json either way -- the model proposes variations within
#      published categories and never invents the statistical structure.
#   2. The movement code for each hypothesis, written per sandbox. Without it
#      every batch runs the hand-written family template and reports
#      generated:false.
#   3. The extraction that turns a 999 call into the report card. Without it
#      intake replays the recorded call and the payload is tagged
#      source:"fallback", so a replay is never presented as a live call.
#
# The search radius is NOT one of these. It is derived from ISRID quantiles
# keyed on the extracted category; the model reads the call, the statistics
# come from the data.
#
OPENAI_API_KEY=


# --- PARALLEL_API_KEY ------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, and needed once rather than per run. https://parallel.ai
#
# Buys: `python orchestrator/local_knowledge.py` runs a web research pass over
# this mountain range and distils it into data/local_knowledge.json, which is
# committed. Hypothesis generation reads that file; the API is never called
# during a run. Findings whose URL is not in the search results are dropped,
# so an on-screen citation can be checked.
#
# The committed file was produced this way on 2026-08-30. Leave this blank
# unless you want to regenerate it.
#
PARALLEL_API_KEY=


# --- OPENTOPO_API_KEY ------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, and needed only to rebuild data/ from source.
# https://opentopography.org -- free account, key arrives by email.
#
# Buys: `python pipeline/fetch_terrain.py elevation` re-downloads the USGS
# 3DEP elevation model. The four arrays it produces are committed, so a clone
# never needs this. Trails and water come from OpenStreetMap and need no key.
#
OPENTOPO_API_KEY=
